# Containers can be used to run databases as well.

# Docker volumes can be used to persist the data. independent of the container lifecycles

# We cannot attach a volume to an existing container.
# A volume can be shared to multiple containers.

| docker volume create mydata | to create a volume |

| docker volume ls | list of volumes |

| docker volume inspect mydata | details of the volume |

# the data will be stored in the sever(ebs in this case)

| docker run -itd --name cont1 --mount src=mydata,destination=/pavan/ ubuntu | to mount the created volume in the container's mentioned path |

# volumes path is in the docker's default path which is /var/lib/docker/
# for jenkins: /var/lib/jenkins/

